SPECIALIST PLAN:
Plan: Visit in order: 1) nearest rock, 2) nearest container, 3) nearest car. Roles and steps:

Navigator:
- Wait for a centroid from lidar for the current target class.
- When given a centroid, navigate to a goal that is the centroid offset at least 3.0 m toward the spawn (0,0) (or toward a provided free-cell anchor if map used). Do not navigate to the centroid itself.
- Report success/failure after each navigate_to_pose. A successful arrival (~within 2.5 m) is enough.

Lidar:
- When stationary and requested, run semantic lidar scan for the current target class and return any object centroids and class labels visible.
- If a centroid for the requested class is returned, supply it so nav can compute a safe 3+ m offset goal.
- After navigator reports success for a stop, call confirm_stop(<class>) to validate the stop. If confirm_stop returns false or lidar did not see the object, report that and allow camera to attempt confirm_stop.

Camera:
- When stationary and requested, take an RGB (and optional class histogram) and report if it sees the requested class.
- If lidar cannot confirm a stop, attempt confirm_stop(<class>) as a fallback.

Failure / exploration policy:
- If lidar scan returns no centroid for the current target class, request occupancy map and pick a free-cell viewpoint at least 3 m away from any previously-seen centroid and navigate there, then repeat the lidar scan.
- If a navigate_to_pose fails twice with the same goal, pick a different nearby free-cell anchor (via occupancy map) and try a different goal.

Stop rule:
- Proceed to the next target only after confirm_stop(<class>) returns true for the current target.
- Report mission done only after all three classes have been confirmed.

Please AGREE or DISAGREE.
